  "solution": {
    "text": "Perpendicular distance of centre $\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 0,-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$ from $x+2 y-2=4$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\left|\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}-4\\right|}{\\sqrt{6}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\\n& \\text { radius }=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}}=1 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
